# Playing with History.

**Authors:** Solomon, Gwen

## Abstract
Discusses types of software most useful in social studies classes--games, simulations, and word processing, database, spreadsheets, and graphing--and introduces applications software through descriptions of four learning activities from different parts of the social studies curriculum: introducing databases, writing historical journals, tracking immigration with spreadsheets, and microcomputers in microeconomics. (MBR)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ341653

